From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] readline: implement _rl_erase_entire_line, add rl_clear_visible_line and rl_reset_line_state

These GNU Readline (>= 8.1) functions are part of the Readline API to
erase the current prompt line before printing asynchronous output and to
reset the line display state.

Implement _rl_erase_entire_line() using libedit's re_clear_lines() and
re_clear_display(), wrap it in rl_clear_visible_line(), and implement
rl_reset_line_state() via re_clear_display().

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN a/src/editline/readline.h b/src/editline/readline.h
--- a/src/editline/readline.h	2026-05-08 15:40:44.000000000 -0400
+++ b/src/editline/readline.h	2026-09-17 20:36:17.926627708 -0400
@@ -252,6 +252,8 @@
     __attribute__((__format__(__printf__, 1, 2)));
 void		 rl_save_prompt(void);
 void		 rl_restore_prompt(void);
+void		 rl_clear_visible_line(void);
+int		 rl_reset_line_state(void);
 
 /*
  * The following are not implemented
diff -ruN a/src/readline.c b/src/readline.c
--- a/src/readline.c	2026-05-08 15:40:44.000000000 -0400
+++ b/src/readline.c	2026-09-17 20:36:22.567802249 -0400
@@ -2628,4 +2628,26 @@
 void
 _rl_erase_entire_line(void)
 {
+	if (h == NULL || e == NULL)
+		rl_initialize();
+
+	re_clear_lines(e);
+	re_clear_display(e);
+	terminal__flush(e);
+}
+
+void
+rl_clear_visible_line(void)
+{
+	_rl_erase_entire_line();
+}
+
+int
+rl_reset_line_state(void)
+{
+	if (h == NULL || e == NULL)
+		rl_initialize();
+
+	re_clear_display(e);
+	return 0;
 }
